## Interlude / Side B — English Translation: Chapters 13–16

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 13 — Searching for Echoes Next Door
################################################################################

translate en b13_001:
    "Three days had passed since that afternoon in the library. Tomorrow's cassettes still played, still turned out right. But what kept looping in Kai's head now wasn't any prediction — it was the crash of a stack of books, and a girl with a boom mic staring flatly at him."

translate en b13_002:
    kai_hati "I don't know her name. Don't know what class she's in. All I know is she records weird sounds, and because of her… I didn't end up dying on Friday. {i}(pause){/i} Sounds crazy. Still can't get it out of my head, though."

translate en b13_003:
    kai_hati "Tomorrow at school… what do I do?"

translate en b13_004a:
    "Kai sat in the corner of the canteen, stirring his iced tea without ever taking a sip. His ears were doing all the work — catching his classmates' chatter. Finally, he worked up the nerve to fish for info."

translate en b13_005a:
    kai "Hey… do you guys know who that kid is? The one who always brings recording gear to the library. The one with the huge headphones, lho."

translate en b13_006a:
    teman1 "Oh, that weird kid from the class next door? XI-Social?"

translate en b13_007a:
    teman2 "Yara. Her name's Yara. Everyone in our grade calls her \"Weird Girl\", rek."

translate en b13_008a:
    kai "Weird how?"

translate en b13_009a:
    teman2 "Well, every single day she just wears giant headphones and wanders around school carrying a long mic. Yesterday I saw her crouching by the gutter. Recording water sounds, she said. Totally random, right? {i}(chuckles){/i}"

translate en b13_010a:
    teman1 "Heard she collects pointless background noise like that."

translate en b13_011a:
    "The conversation moved on to that afternoon's soccer match. Kai didn't laugh along. He set down his iced tea glass, condensation already beading on the sides."

translate en b13_012a:
    kai_hati "Yara. {i}(repeating it quietly to himself){/i} Her name is Yara. Short. Like a missed beat in an unfinished song."

translate en b13_013a:
    "On his way back to class, Kai made a point of walking past XI-Social. Hanging on the board near the door was their classroom duty roster — and on the Thursday row, there was that same name. YARA."

translate en b13_014a:
    kai_hati "Really is Yara. Okay. Tomorrow I'll say hi. Tomorrow. For sure."

translate en b13_004b:
    "Kai didn't ask anyone. Didn't dare walk past XI-Social either. He just went through his day like normal — or tried to look normal."

translate en b13_005b:
    kai_hati "If we're supposed to run into each other again, this school isn't that big. We will. {i}(pause){/i} …Hopefully we will."

translate en b13_006b:
    "Strangely though, there was no sign of giant headphones or a long microphone anywhere all day. And Kai walked home with a feeling he refused to call disappointment."

translate en b13_004c:
    "For a whole week, Kai took the long way around. The east corridor was farther from his classroom — but it didn't go past the library."

translate en b13_005c:
    kai_hati "Not scared. I just… don't want a repeat of yesterday. Normal people don't laugh like a maniac in the library just because they didn't die. {i}(pause){/i} Bottom line, stay away from there for now."

translate en b13_006c:
    "On the eighth day, a group assignment forced him back. And the library had changed a little: the seat by the window — her seat — was taken by someone else now. Apparently she'd changed her usual hours."

translate en b13_007c:
    kai_hati "…Well. Changed her schedule. {i}(sits down, opening a book without really reading){/i} Whatever. That's what I wanted anyway, right?"

translate en b13_015:
    "The bell rang. Kai walked down the XI-Social hallway — today his class actually had to pass this way — and slowed his steps as he passed the wide-open doorway."

translate en b13_016:
    "There she was. By the window, very back row. The girl sat with her chin resting on her hand, watching the light drizzle fall over the school field. Big black headphones hung around her neck. Her fingers toyed with a small pocket recorder on the desk. Her classmates were throwing paper balls and shouting across the room — yet none of it seemed to reach her."

translate en b13_017:
    kai_hati "That's her. So calm. Like there's a glass wall around her, and she's the only one who knows it's there."

translate en b13_018:
    "The girl turned her head. Their eyes met across the noisy hallway. She frowned slightly — recognizing Kai: the guy who'd laughed like he was possessed in the library."

translate en b13_019a:
    yara "{i}(stares at him flatly, then speaks just loud enough for him to hear){/i} …You're the one who was asking around about me at the canteen yesterday, aren't you?"

translate en b13_020a:
    kai "{i}(freezes){/i} H-huh?! How did you—"

translate en b13_021a:
    yara "Small school. {i}(looks back out the window){/i} Next time you're curious, just ask me directly."

translate en b13_019b:
    "Yara looked at him flatly for a few seconds. Not angry, not smiling. Then she turned back to the window, as if Kai were just one more sound in a noisy hallway."

translate en b13_019c:
    yara "{i}(raises an eyebrow){/i} Oh. Still alive, I see."

translate en b13_020c:
    kai "…Huh?"

translate en b13_021c:
    yara "Didn't see you in the library all week. {i}(looks back out the window){/i} Thought the Boy Waiting to Die had actually died."

translate en b13_022:
    "Kai took a deep breath. His heart was hammering — but not out of fear this time. It felt different. It felt like… a beginning."

translate en b13_023:
    kai_hati "Yesterday I was walking toward the end of everything. Today… feels like I'm walking toward something new. Something noisy. {i}(smiles faintly){/i} And I want to learn what it's about."

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 14 — Melody from a Boiling Pot
################################################################################

translate en b14_001:
    "The canteen was ridiculously loud that afternoon. Clinking spoons, kids laughing in the corner, stall vendors shouting out orders — all piling on top of each other."

translate en b14_002:
    "Yet right in the middle of the chaos, Yara was like a quiet island. In the corner of the canteen, near the noodle stall, she was crouched down. Her big headphones sat halfway on — left ear covered, right ear open. Her hand was steady, pointing a small microphone at a massive aluminum pot on top of a roaring gas burner. Thick white steam billowed up."

translate en b14_003a:
    kai_hati "Okay. Yesterday she said: just ask directly. {i}(takes a breath){/i} Be direct. No more beating around the bush."

translate en b14_003b:
    kai_hati "See. Ran into her after all. {i}(swallows){/i} …Now what? Not like I can just watch from afar again."

translate en b14_003c:
    kai_hati "She's here. Not in the library. {i}(pause){/i} Spent a whole week dodging her, and of course I run into her in the canteen. The universe has a terrible sense of humor."

translate en b14_004:
    "Kai stepped carefully, trying not to let his shoes squeak on the slick canteen floor. His throat suddenly felt dry. Weird — usually he stressed about tomorrow. This time he was nervous about right now."

translate en b14_005:
    kai "{i}(softly, almost a whisper){/i} …What are you doing?"

translate en b14_006:
    "Yara didn't flinch. She glanced back over her shoulder, recognized Kai, then returned her eyes to the bubbling water in the pot."

translate en b14_007:
    yara "Recording boiling water. {i}(without looking over){/i} Be quiet for a second. The frequency's really good right now."

translate en b14_008:
    "Kai shut his mouth immediately. He crouched down beside Yara, keeping enough space so he wouldn't bump her elbow."

translate en b14_009:
    kai_hati "Bloop… bloop-bloop… bloop. Bubbles knocking against the sides of the pot. Nearly a full minute of the two of us squatting in this hot corner of the canteen. And weirdly enough… I don't mind."

translate en b14_010:
    "Yara hit stop. She let out a satisfied breath, slipped her headphones down around her neck, and turned to face Kai with one eyebrow raised."

translate en b14_011:
    yara "You again. The guy who laughed like he was possessed yesterday. {i}(eyes him){/i} Why are you following me now?"

translate en b14_012:
    kai "I'm not following you. {i}(looks away toward an empty noodle bowl on a nearby table){/i} I'm just… curious. Why record boiling water? Isn't that just… ordinary noise?"

translate en b14_013:
    "Before Yara could answer, the pot on the next burner started boiling even harder — and the noodle stall vendor struggled to lift a second, smaller pot."

translate en b14_014a:
    "Kai pulled his phone from his pocket, opened the voice recorder app, and aimed it at the pot. His hand shook a little, but the recording was rolling."

translate en b14_015a:
    yara "{i}(glances at Kai's phone, eyebrow ticking up){/i} …What are you doing?"

translate en b14_016a:
    kai "U-uh, just… messing around. I mean, the sound is… pretty decent, right?"

translate en b14_017a:
    yara "{i}(holding back a smile){/i} Messing around. Huh. Well, save it properly. Never know when it might come in handy."

translate en b14_014b:
    "Kai stayed crouched and quiet, letting the bubbling sound wash over him as it was. He didn't save anything except his own memory of it."

translate en b14_015b:
    yara "{i}(watches Kai for a beat){/i} Turns out you know how to stay quiet after all."

translate en b14_016b:
    kai "…Just learning."

translate en b14_014c:
    kai "Bu, let me help you with that, Bu— {i}(lifts the side of the pot together with the stall vendor){/i} …There. Careful, it's hot."

translate en b14_015c:
    ibu_penjual "Lho, thanks, Le. Rare to see a kid jump in to help. {i}(scoops extra toppings into Kai's waiting bowl){/i} Here, on the house. Don't tell anyone."

translate en b14_016c:
    yara "{i}(looks at Kai, her tone softening){/i} …Are you always like that? See someone struggling and just jump right in?"

translate en b14_017c:
    kai "Not always. Sometimes it's just… reflex, I guess."

translate en b14_018:
    "Yara looked at the pot still puffing steam beside them, then shifted her gaze back to Kai's face. Her look was sharp, yet deep."

translate en b14_019:
    yara "Everyone calls it noise, Kai."

translate en b14_020:
    kai "…You know my name?"

translate en b14_021:
    yara "You were asking around about me at the canteen yesterday, remember? {i}(smiles faintly){/i} Only fair I asked around too. — Everyone calls it noise. But to this recorder, it's an honest song."

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 15 — Honesty Beneath the Noise
################################################################################

translate en b15_001:
    "Yara coiled her mic cable with calm, practiced motions. Right in the middle of the noisy canteen, it was like she had her own pocket of quiet that nobody could break into."

translate en b15_002:
    yara "I'm collecting these sounds for a portfolio. {i}(pats her canvas bag stuffed with recording gear){/i} I want to major in music arts. Not the usual kind they teach at school, though."

translate en b15_003:
    kai "{i}(frowns, still crouched){/i} Not the usual kind? You mean… not a band, not an orchestra?"

translate en b15_004:
    yara "{i}(gives a soft scoff, half cynical, half sweet){/i} I hate pop music that's too neat. Tidy melodies, predictable chords, forced syrupy lyrics. To me, all of that feels… fake."

translate en b15_005:
    "She held up her pocket recorder right in front of Kai's face."

translate en b15_006:
    yara "I prefer noise. Honest noise. {i}(her eyes light up){/i} Boiling water. The creak of an unoiled library door. Truck tires gripping wet asphalt. None of them pretend to sound pretty. They make a sound simply because they exist."

translate en b15_007:
    kai_hati "Weird. The way she explains it feels completely foreign. Still, some part of my chest… agrees. I'm sick of a world where everything's scripted, rushed, forced to go a certain way, too."

translate en b15_008:
    yara "{i}(looks straight at Kai){/i} The world is loud, Kai. If you only want to listen to the pretty parts… you're basically deaf to half of life."

translate en b15_009:
    "The sentence hit Kai slowly, like a wave rolling in."

translate en b15_010:
    kai_hati "Deaf to half of life… What have I been doing all this time? Using those cassettes to filter tomorrow. Only wanting to hear what's certain. What's safe. Everything else — I shut my ears tight against it. {i}(pause){/i} Including… surprises like meeting her."

translate en b15_011:
    kai "{i}(quietly, staring off){/i} Deaf to half of life…"

translate en b15_012:
    yara "{i}(stands up, dusting off her gray skirt from the floor){/i} What? Hit a nerve?"

translate en b15_013:
    kai "{i}(scrambles to stand up too){/i} No— well… a little. {i}(scratches his head){/i} Just a tiny bit. Okay, fine, quite a lot."

translate en b15_014:
    yara "{i}(laughs softly){/i} Honest at last. — By the way, I'm curious about one thing. {i}(eyes him closely){/i} What's the sound you hate the most?"

translate en b15_015:
    kai "Huh? Where'd that come from?"

translate en b15_016:
    yara "Everyone has one. Come on. Just say the first thing that pops into your head, don't overthink it. That's the honest answer."

translate en b15_017a:
    kai "The school bell. Seriously. It sounds like… an order. \"Alright, time to be scared again.\""

translate en b15_018a:
    yara "{i}(nods slowly){/i} The school bell. Okay. Noted."

translate en b15_017b:
    kai "People whispering. Sounds like they're hiding something… and usually whatever they're hiding is about me. {i}(laughs dryly){/i} Sounds paranoid, huh."

translate en b15_018b:
    yara "A little. {i}(smiles){/i} Honest, though. Noted."

translate en b15_017c:
    kai "{i}(pause){/i} Silence. Total quiet. Whenever a room goes completely silent… my head immediately fills it in with all the worst thoughts."

translate en b15_018c:
    yara "{i}(looks at him longer than usual){/i} …Silence. Okay. That one… I'll remember carefully."

translate en b15_019:
    yara "{i}(tucks the recorder into her canvas bag, getting ready to leave){/i} Alright. Bell's about to ring. I need to return some gear to the art room."

translate en b15_020:
    kai_hati "She's leaving. The conversation's over. {i}(pause){/i} …I don't want it to be over. For once, I talked to someone and tomorrow didn't feel like a threat. Tomorrow felt like… a blank page. One I want to listen to with her."

translate en b15_021:
    kai "Oh— right, okay. Take care. {i}(after Yara takes two steps){/i} …Yara."

translate en b15_022:
    yara "{i}(stops, glancing back){/i} Hm?"

translate en b15_023:
    kai "{i}(opens his mouth, closes it again, then finally:){/i} Nothing. Never mind. See you around."

translate en b15_024:
    yara "{i}(shrugs, smiling faintly){/i} You definitely will. Small school."

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 16 — When Noise Becomes a Symphony
################################################################################

translate en b16_001:
    "The next afternoon, without even planning it, Kai's feet carried him back to that same corner of the canteen. Yara was already there — not crouched this time, just standing and aiming her mic out into the crowd, like someone fishing in a rushing river."

translate en b16_002:
    yara "{i}(without turning around){/i} You again."

translate en b16_003:
    kai "You always know, huh."

translate en b16_004:
    yara "I can hear your footsteps. Everyone else walks like they're in a rush. You… walk like you're asking the floor for permission. {i}(turns around to face him){/i} Come here."

translate en b16_005:
    kai "Huh? Come here for what—"

translate en b16_006:
    yara "Put these on."

translate en b16_007:
    "Before Kai could even process it, Yara stepped closer and slipped her big black headphones over his ears. Quick, no asking first. There was still a faint warmth left in the ear cushions — from where she'd just been wearing them."

translate en b16_008:
    "And the world shifted. The canteen's din, usually just one messy lump of noise, suddenly unraveled into crisp, detailed layers. Through the sensitive mic in Yara's hand, Kai heard things that had always slipped right past him."

translate en b16_009:
    kai_hati "That's… rain on the tin roof. Sounds like percussion. Random, yet patterned."

translate en b16_010:
    kai_hati "Car horns. From here they actually sound like… a sad melody stuck in traffic."

translate en b16_011:
    kai_hati "Footsteps. Everybody's. So close, so textured… like they're dancing right inside my head."

translate en b16_012:
    "Kai closed his eyes. For the first time, the noise of the world didn't make him anxious. Guided by Yara's ears, he started hearing music inside the chaos."

translate en b16_013:
    yara "{i}(her voice sounds distant from outside the headphones){/i} Well? Still think it's just useless noise?"

translate en b16_014:
    "Kai opened his eyes slowly. He took the headphones off and handed them back to Yara. Then he smiled — a genuine smile that rarely ever showed up on his face."

translate en b16_015:
    kai "No. That was… amazing. Felt like there's a whole other world I've never heard before. {i}(pause){/i} And it's just been sitting right there, every single day. I just never listened."

translate en b16_016:
    yara "{i}(smiles, pleased){/i} See? Turns out the Boy Waiting to Die can listen after all."

translate en b16_017:
    kai "You're still calling me that, huh."

translate en b16_018:
    yara "A good nickname's hard to drop. {i}(packs up her gear){/i} Besides, you haven't given me a reason to change it yet."

translate en b16_019:
    "Yara slung her heavy canvas bag over her shoulder — tripod, cables, spare recorder — and started walking away as usual. Three steps in, she stopped."

translate en b16_020:
    yara "{i}(without turning back){/i} Tomorrow I'm heading under the overpass near the station. The echo there is wild. {i}(pause){/i} Day after that, the market. After that… who knows. My hunting schedule's packed."

translate en b16_021:
    kai_hati "She's talking to me. That's not small talk. That's… {i}(swallows){/i} That's a door. A door she cracked open just a bit. Up to me whether I have the guts to walk through."

translate en b16_022a:
    kai "{i}(quickly, before his nerve runs out){/i} Starting tomorrow, I'm coming with you. Your bag's heavy, right? Let me carry it. You just hold the mic."

translate en b16_023a:
    yara "{i}(turns around, looks at him for a long beat — then breaks into a wide smile for the very first time){/i} …Deal. Three o'clock, school gate. One minute late and I'm leaving without you."

translate en b16_024a:
    kai "Won't be late."

translate en b16_025a:
    yara "We'll see. {i}(starts walking off, then half-shouts without looking back){/i} And leave your tomorrow tapes at home. Tomorrow doesn't need spoilers."

translate en b16_026a:
    kai_hati "…She knows about the tapes? {i}(chuckles quietly to himself){/i} Whatever. Tomorrow I'm going with her. Tomorrow, just this once, I don't want to know what's coming first."

translate en b16_022b:
    kai "If I have time… I'll tag along. Can't promise every day, though. Some days I have to— {i}(cuts himself off){/i} …yeah, just whenever I have time."

translate en b16_023b:
    yara "{i}(gives a single, flat nod){/i} Okay. Whenever you have time."

translate en b16_024b:
    "She didn't ask twice. Kai watched her back disappear into the crowd, and those words \"whenever I have time\" hung in the canteen air — like an unfinished sentence."

translate en b16_025b:
    kai_hati "Why does my mouth always slam the brakes first."

translate en b16_022c:
    kai "Sounds fun… but that's your world, Yar. I don't know a thing about that stuff. {i}(smiles stiffly){/i} I'll just listen to the finished recordings later, okay?"

translate en b16_023c:
    yara "{i}(pauses briefly, then shrugs){/i} Alright. The finished recordings. {i}(walks off){/i}"

translate en b16_024c:
    "Yara walked away alone, the heavy canvas bag on her shoulder, boom mic sticking out as usual. To Kai's ears, the canteen went right back to being ordinary noise."

translate en b16_025c:
    kai_hati "…Weird. I just turned down the exact thing I actually really wanted to do. And I don't even know why."

translate en b16_027a:
    "From that afternoon on, Kai had a new destination after school. Not his bedroom, not that damp alley — wherever Yara and her microphone went. He hauled the heavy canvas bag full of tripods and cables under the overpass, through the bustling traditional market, to the city park at dusk."

translate en b16_027a_p2:
    "Yara walked ahead, boom mic raised like a hunter tracking a rare creature. Kai trailed behind carrying her gear — and laughing more often than he remembered ever doing."

translate en b16_027b:
    "From that afternoon on, there were days Kai tagged along — carrying Yara's canvas bag to the market, to the city park — and days he didn't show up, without a word. Yara never asked why."

translate en b16_027b_p2:
    "She just always started five minutes later on the days Kai came, as if leaving room for him. And on the days he didn't, she recorded on her own, just like before. Like before Kai was ever there."

translate en b16_027c:
    "From that afternoon on, not much changed — on the surface. Yara kept hunting sounds on her own, and every so often, in the canteen or the library, she'd play the finished recordings for Kai through one side of her headphones."

translate en b16_027c_p2:
    "Kai listened, praised them sincerely… then went home, played tomorrow's cassette, and wondered why that praise felt like watching someone else's life through glass."

translate en b16_028:
    kai_hati "Turns out the world really can slow down. Not always — but it can. {i}(pause){/i} And funny thing, I just realized: lately I haven't been going to Pak Ageng's shop because I'm panicking. Sometimes it's just because… I want to tell him about my day."
